(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111. `Set element N of L to <collection>.` was not
 individually named by the ruling's own enumeration (literal, append, map
 insert, read-out), but the same principle applies to any write into an
 existing slot; extended here for consistency.)

a list called inner is [1, 2].
a list called outer is [0, 0].
Set element 1 of outer to inner.
Set element 1 of inner to 777.
print outer.
print inner.
